Safety factors should take into account potential risks related to:
• the novelty of the active substance;
• its pharmacodynamic characteristics, including irreversible or long lasting findings and the shape of the dose-response curve;
• the relevance of the animal models used for safety testing;
• the characteristics of the safety findings;
• uncertainties related to the estimation of the MABEL, PAD and the expected exposure in humans.
